# Commerce AI Tool

AI-powered product search plugin for commercetools (text, voice, image). pnpm + Turborepo monorepo.

## Packages

- `packages/core` — business logic, AI (OpenRouter/Bedrock), commercetools client (`src/search/*` pipelines, `src/browser/*` shared client logic exported as `@commerce-ai-tool/core/client`)
- `packages/server` — Next.js/Express handlers, ElevenLabs STT/TTS (`routes.ts` is the single route table)
- `packages/react` — React search widget (glass UI)
- `packages/angular` — Angular widget components and services (ng-packagr, partial compilation)
- `packages/styles` — shared widget CSS (private)
- `apps/demo-next` — Next.js 16 demo app
- `apps/demo-angular` — Angular 21 demo app with a standalone Express BFF (`:4200` → `:3002`)

Dependencies: `server` / `react` / `angular` → `core`. `core`, `server`, `react`, `angular` are one fixed Changesets group. API secrets stay on the server only.

## Stack

TypeScript 7 native (`packages/angular` and `demo-angular` stay on `typescript ~5.9` for the Angular compiler), tsup (ng-packagr for Angular), Vitest 5, Playwright E2E, ESLint 10, Turbo 2, Changesets, pnpm 11.22.0, Node ≥ 24.

## Architecture

```
Browser → /api/commerce-ai/* (server) → core → AI + commercetools
```

Product cards after Product Search are hydrated via commercetools GraphQL (`products` query for name/image/price/sku).

React and Angular widgets configure microphone, camera capture, and image upload independently through `enableVoice`, `enableCameraSearch`, and `enableImageSearch`.

Checkout is host-routed: `CommerceAISearch.onCheckout` navigates to a host page that can render `CommerceAICheckout`. Server checkout routes set addresses, list/select matching shipping methods, authorize payment through a host-injected `PaymentProvider` (commercetools Payment + `addPayment`), and create an Order from the Active Cart. `GET /orders` lists recent orders for the current session; `GET /orders?orderNumber=` returns confirmation and tracking for that order.

Shopping missions (opt-in `enableMissions` / `CAT_MISSIONS_*`) split compound text, voice, and image queries into product intents, search in parallel, and batch-add via `POST /cart/add-items`.

Never expose API keys in client-side code.

